# UNI-305: a six-tenant, UNEQUAL-weight set whose worker counts deliberately
# do NOT encode the weights. Equal workers (32 each) against a 40/20/15/10/10/5
# split puts every tenant's worker share at 16.7% against weight shares of
# 5-40%, a 46.7pt total gap -- so a PASS here is the policy reallocating the
# pool, not the load generator having already done it
# ([[pass_rows_are_worker_sized_to_weights]]). Weights are UNI-187's `graded`
# set (epp-groups/render.py); identities are its app1..app6 table.
#
# Render the matching EPP config with
#   python3 -I deploy/poc/tenants.py render-config deploy/poc/tenants/six-unequal.tenants
#
# group  weight  match                  keys             workers  rate  shape
app1     40      exact:app1-production  app1-production  32       -     -
app2     20      exact:app2-batch       app2-batch       32       -     -
app3     15      exact:app3             app3             32       -     -
app4     10      exact:app4             app4             32       -     -
app5     10      exact:app5             app5             32       -     -
app6     5       exact:app6             app6             32       -     -
